{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"submission\":\"update.json\",\"summary\":\"Answered the restart question's last open point from source and corrected a precision error in the first draft of that claim. send_accsync sets the follower's valid entries index to its reported accepted index (3) when the promise matches the leader's ballot, to min(previous round maximum, 3) when it matches the earlier round, and to the follower's decided index (4) otherwise; create_log_sync starts the suffix there and sync_log rewrites only from sync_idx onward. The hole at index 2 therefore survives whenever the promise round's maximum accepted index is 3 or more, which the witness's peers supply with accepted 37; a maximum of 2 or below would place the boundary at index 2 and rewrite it. Recorded that conditional bound as behavior, attached it to the restart question, and restated the account with it. Validation is valid with execution_requested false; the bound remains source-derived, assumes the non-snapshot sync path, and the recovery messages were never delivered.\"}"}}
